ediately.'}]}, {'group': 'Valid subschema, walk enabled, OpenAPI3 disabled – early success after walk', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'executionContext', 'value': 'mockExecutionContext_success_walk_noDiscriminator'}, {'parameter': 'node', 'value': 'mockNode_array'}, {'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': 'mockRootNode_array'}, {'parameter': 'instanceLocation', 'value': 'mockInstanceLocation_root'}], 'expected': 'empty Set<ValidationMessage>', 'description': 'State.isWalkEnabled() returns true, schema.walk() returns an empty set, state.hasMatchedNode() is true. With OpenAPI3 discriminators disabled the method clears allErrors and returns the empty set.'}]}, {'group': 'OpenAPI3 discriminator match found, errors present', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'executionContext', 'value': 'mockExecutionContext_errors_discriminatorMatch'}, {'parameter': 'node', 'value': 'mockNode_object'}, {'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': 'mockRootNode_object'}, {'parameter': 'instanceLocation', 'value': 'mockInstanceLocation_root'}], 'expected': 'Set containing original error(s) plus a DISCRIMINATOR_REMARK ValidationMessage', 'description': 'OpenAPI3 style discriminators are enabled and discriminatorContext.isDiscriminatorMatchFound() returns true. The subschema validation produces errors. The method must add those errors, append the discriminator remark, and return the (non‑empty) error set.'}]}, {'group': 'OpenAPI3 discriminator match found, no errors', 'cases': [{'input': [{'parameter': 'executionContext', 'value': 'mockExecutionContext_success_discriminatorMatch'}, {'parameter': 'node', 'value': 'mockNode_object'}, {'parameter': 'rootNode', 'value': 'mockRootNode_object'}, {'parameter': 'instanceLocation', 'value': 'mockInstanceLocation_root'}], 'expected': 'empty Set<ValidationMessage>', 'description': 'OpenAPI3 discriminators enabled, discriminator match found, but the subschema validates without errors. The method clears allErrors and returns an empty set.'}]}, {'group': 'After l